From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:47:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: embedder ignores QEMU_* option variables

Embedded in a host application, linux-user's main runs in that
application's process, so getenv() reads the application's
environment: a QEMU_CPU, QEMU_STRACE, QEMU_LD_PREFIX or
QEMU_GUEST_BASE meant for anything else reconfigures the emulator
under the embedder's argv. The embedder's argv is the whole
configuration: parse_args no longer reads the arg_table variables.
Removing them from the environment instead would race other host
threads' getenv().

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedding is ATL-only]
Patch-Reason: in-process QEMU shares the host process environment; argv alone must configure it
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 linux-user/main.c | 15 +++++----------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/linux-user/main.c b/linux-user/main.c
index 60a695b7ca3e9f79406436219fb0ad7896ad6b6d..5c22ad999afc555979c5abff48c4c447f20aee8c 100644
--- a/linux-user/main.c
+++ b/linux-user/main.c
@@ -615,16 +615,11 @@ static int parse_args(int argc, char **argv)
     int optind;
     const struct qemu_argument *arginfo;
 
-    for (arginfo = arg_table; arginfo->handle_opt != NULL; arginfo++) {
-        if (arginfo->env == NULL) {
-            continue;
-        }
-
-        r = getenv(arginfo->env);
-        if (r != NULL) {
-            arginfo->handle_opt(r);
-        }
-    }
+    /*
+     * Embedded: the embedder's argv is the whole configuration. The
+     * QEMU_* option variables live in the host process's environment,
+     * which belongs to the embedding application, not to QEMU.
+     */
 
     optind = 1;
     for (;;) {
